    "Tajweed (تجويد) refers to the science and practice of reciting the Quran correctly and beautifully, by giving each letter its proper articulation and characteristics. Linguistically, the word tajweed comes from the Arabic root ج-و-د (j-w-d), meaning \"to improve,\" \"to make excellent,\" or \"to perfect.\" In the context of the Quran, it means reciting the words of Allah as they were revealed precisely, clearly, and with care." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale"
    },
    "Tajweed (تَجوِيد) refers to the science and practice of reciting the Quran correctly and beautifully, by giving each letter its proper articulation and characteristics." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "التجويد علمٌ وعملٌ في تلاوة القرآن تلاوةً صحيحة حسنة، بإعطاء كل حرف حقه من المخرج والصفات."
          }
        },
        "ur" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "تجوید (تَجوِيد) سے مراد قرآن مجید کو درست اور خوبصورت انداز میں پڑھنے کا علم اور عمل ہے، جس میں ہر حرف کو اس کا صحیح مخرج اور صفات دی جاتی ہیں۔"
          }
        }
      }
    },
