    "There is a habit that separates a reader who has memorised rules from one who can actually use them. The first meets a word, retrieves the rule from memory, and applies it. The second looks at the word and sees that something is already marked. Both arrive at the same recitation, but only the second is reading. This lesson is about the second habit, and it costs nothing to learn: the marks are already on every page you have ever opened." : {
