    "There is a third place where بَلۡ meets a ر, and it does not merge: كَلَّاۖ بَلۡۜ رَانَ in Surat al-Mutaffifin. Hafs, by the way of ash-Shatibiyyah, reads a sakt there, a brief cut of the voice without taking a breath, and a merge cannot cross a silence, so both the ل and the ر are heard. It is one of the four sakts read in this riwayah, along with عِوَجَاۜ in al-Kahf, مَّرۡقَدِنَاۜ in Ya-Sin, and مَنۡۜ رَاقٖ in al-Qiyamah. The mark ـۜ printed above the line is what tells you. A fifth place, مَالِيَهۡ running into هَلَكَ at the end of al-Haaqqah, is related two ways, and the next lesson takes it up." : {
